   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, independent of the author): REQUEST CHANGES** — head b32dce431b4c1fcd6e5a8ef70a004d09b9b3e449\n\n1. **Medium** (LESSONS 2), `ModeratorAlertModelTests.swift:206-214`: the new test passes on `dev-swift` without the change; it never reads the build setting. Fix: assert `ModeratorAlertMail.address(from: Bundle.main.infoDictionary ?? [:]) != nil` (app-hosted tests), show it fails with the line emptied.\n2. **Medium**, upgrade trap: an old copy of `Secrets.xcconfig.example` has an uncommented empty `MODERATOR_ALERT_MAIL_ADDRESS =` that silently overrides the shared value and turns the fallback off, including in release builds made on the maintainer's Mac. Fix: say so in the PR body and `App/README.md`.\n3. **Low** (LESSONS 3), stale text: `ModeratorAlertModel.swift:119-120` (\"a third party's address stays out of source\"), `LOT-071-third-party-services.md:71-72`, `App/README.md:43` (values empty without Secrets).\n4. **Nit**, `App/README.md:40`: an override with a real address replaces it; only an empty value turns it off.\n\n**Checked**: address and line 4580 match legacy exactly; subject/body legacy's; xcconfig → Info-Keys.plist → `AppEnvironment.swift:57` flow; `#include?` order lets Secrets override; no ledger entry needed (GAP-070 row untouched); ADR sentence present; no secret; all 58 LESSONS rows read (2, 3 fail as above).\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
